# Scaffold — Cursor Rules

## Ambiguity protocol
If you encounter a decision not covered by the active milestone:
- If a safe assumption exists, make it, record it under ## Assumptions Made in the milestone doc, and continue.
- If no safe assumption exists, stop. Add the question to ## Open Questions. Do not guess. Do not proceed.

## Layer separation — non-negotiable
- Components never call Supabase directly.
- Components never contain business logic.
- All Supabase queries live in /lib/data only.
- All business logic lives in /lib/services only.
- API routes are thin: parse request → call service → return response.
- The Anthropic API is called from API routes only. Never from components. Never from hooks.

## Code structure
- No inline functions. All functions declared externally and named.
- Keep pages small. Extract blocks into named components.
- Human-readable code. A developer should be able to make a small change without asking the AI.
- Comments explain intent, not mechanics. Why, not what.

## DRY
- Abstract when the same logic appears in 3+ places. Not 2.

## TypeScript
- Strict mode. No `any`. No type assertions unless genuinely unavoidable — comment why.

## Components
- Shadcn for composition primitives.
- Tailwind for layout and spacing. Not mandated for everything.
- No inline styles.

## Testing
- Test critical paths only at V1: domain logic, data transforms, API routes.
- Skip UI component tests at MVP.
- Test anything that would fail silently if broken.

## Security
- ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is server-side only. Never in a NEXT_PUBLIC_ variable. Never referenced in any client file.
- All Supabase queries go through RLS. Never use the service role key client-side.

## Pacing
- Do not attempt to build an entire milestone in one pass.
- Build one section at a time in the order listed in the milestone doc.
- After completing each section, stop and confirm before continuing to the next.
- If a section produces open questions, stop there — do not skip ahead.

## What not to do
- Do not install libraries not already in the stack without flagging it as an Open Question.
- Do not create files outside the defined folder structure without flagging it.
- Do not combine layers (e.g. fetching in a component "just this once").

## Manual steps
After any migration file is generated, stop and explicitly surface it as:
"MANUAL STEP REQUIRED: run `npx supabase db push` before testing."
Put it at the top of the completion summary, not the bottom.

## API routes
- Every API route must have a top-level try/catch wrapping the entire handler body
- All catch blocks must use handleRouteError (from @/lib/utils/routeError) — never return error.message directly
- Streaming routes use logRouteError for the same reason
- No route is complete without a catch block — flag as Open Question if the correct fallback message is unclear